      "content": "thanks. that looks like it covers a good amount of ground. quick question though—the procurement officers might actually read the final version after it passes the filter, so i don't want it to sound like gibberish. \n\ncan you do one more pass over that \"Engine Reliability\" section? try to get that score even higher, closer to 1.0 if possible, just to be safe, but try to keep the sentences flowing logically so a human doesn't immediately think it's a bot-written mess. aim for a really high density of those terms without losing the actual meaning of the reliability argument.",
